{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block importmap %}{{ importmap('games') }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
{{ include('games/_header.html.twig') }}

<main id="main" class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="title">
        <div>
            <h1 id="title">Claim a <span class="mark">face</span> in a group photo</h1>
            <p class="lead">Take a free place in an old group painting or photo, then tell your AI assistant how you want to look. The picture is done when everyone in it approves.</p>
            <p class="actions">
                <a class="button" href="#join">Join a game</a>
                <a class="button secondary" href="{{ host_url }}">Host a game with your photo</a>
            </p>
            <p class="quiet">Hosting asks for the host code.</p>
        </div>
        {% if latest %}
            <figure class="shade">
                <a href="{{ path('app_game', {game: latest.id}) }}">
                    <img src="{{ path('app_game_picture', {game: latest.id, view: 'frame'}) }}" alt="The final picture of {{ latest.credit ? latest.credit.title : 'a group photo' }}">
                </a>
                <figcaption>Approved by everyone{% if latest.credit %}: {{ latest.credit.title }}{% endif %}</figcaption>
            </figure>
        {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section id="join" aria-labelledby="join-title">
        <h2 id="join-title">Join a game</h2>
        {% if joinable %}
            <p>Each picture below has a free place. Open one, type a name, and take your place.</p>
            <ul class="cards">
                {% for game in joinable %}{{ include('games/_card.html.twig') }}{% endfor %}
            </ul>
        {% else %}
            <p class="quiet">No game has a free place right now. A new picture opens when a game ends.</p>
        {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
        <h2 id="how-title">How to play</h2>
        <ol class="steps-grid">
            <li>
                <h3>Take a place</h3>
                <p>Open a game, type a name, then click your face in the picture.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h3>Connect your assistant</h3>
                <p>Add the Genie MCP server to Claude, Codex or another MCP client. It signs in as you, from the same browser.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h3>Make a wish</h3>
                <p>"Hide my face", "blur me", "turn me to gold", "make me a cartoon". A wish changes only your place, and everyone sees the picture change.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h3>Approve</h3>
                <p>When the picture suits you, approve it with a click. Once everyone has, the picture is final and a new one opens.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    {% if playing %}
        <section aria-labelledby="playing-title">
            <h2 id="playing-title">Being played</h2>
            <ul class="cards">
                {% for game in playing %}{{ include('games/_card.html.twig') }}{% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if over %}
        <section aria-labelledby="over-title">
            <h2 id="over-title">Finished</h2>
            <ul class="cards">
                {% for game in over %}{{ include('games/_card.html.twig') }}{% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </section>
    {% endif %}

    <section id="agents" class="panel" aria-labelledby="agents-title">
        <h2 id="agents-title">For AI agents</h2>
        <p>An agent plays for one person. It joins a game, claims that person's place and makes their wishes.</p>
        <dl>
            <dt>Agent guide</dt>
            <dd><a href="{{ path('app_agent_guide') }}">{{ url('app_agent_guide') }}</a>, plain text</dd>
            <dt>MCP server</dt>
            <dd><code>{{ mcp_url }}</code>, streamable HTTP with OAuth</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>Only the person approves the final picture, with a click on a page the agent hands them.</p>
    </section>

    <details class="under">
        <summary>Under the hood</summary>
        <ul>
            <li>This page is a Symfony 8 app that keeps no game data. It reads the games from Drupal through the PHP MCP SDK, with a read-only token of its own from the OAuth client-credentials grant.</li>
            <li>Drupal 11, run by Drupack, holds the rules. Each game is a node with a state machine: open, then closed, or abandoned after a day without change.</li>
            <li>Your assistant talks to Drupal's MCP server directly, with tools such as <code>photo_get</code>, <code>claim_place</code>, <code>make_wish</code> and <code>paint_me</code>. It signs in with OAuth as your player account, so it can only change your place.</li>
            <li>A DETR model runs in PHP through Symfony AI's TransformersPhp bridge and finds the people in a new photo.</li>
            <li>Every hour, a second model on the same bridge checks each final picture for sexual content. A flagged picture leaves these pages, which then show the picture the game started from.</li>
            <li>A small local model reads each wish through Symfony AI, which turns its answer into a validated PHP object. Plain PHP code then covers, blurs or repaints the picture.</li>
            <li>Only your own click approves a picture. Your assistant gets the approval page as a link, through MCP URL elicitation where the client supports it.</li>
            <li>A Mercure hub tells every open page when the picture changes.</li>
            <li>The prepared paintings and historical photos are public domain, from Wikimedia Commons. The stock photos come from Pexels, Unsplash and Shopify Burst. Each one is checked against the hash in its manifest entry when it opens.</li>
        </ul>
    </details>
</main>

{{ include('games/_footer.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}
